# Trace the AI Hero survey system end to end

## Step

Establish exactly how a survey works today in the running AI Hero app: how it is
authored, how it is served, how a learner answers it, where the answer lands, and
what API surface exists for an outside agent to drive it.

Read (do not modify) in `~/Code/badass-courses/ai-hero/apps/ai-hero`:

- `src/app/admin/surveys/**` — the whole CRUD surface, including
  `_components/survey-crud-dialog.tsx`, `question-crud-dialog.tsx`,
  `questions-list.tsx`, `survey-settings.tsx`, `survey-responses.tsx`, and
  `src/app/admin/surveys/[slug]/**`.
- `src/lib/surveys-api.ts`, `src/lib/surveys.ts`, `src/lib/surveys-query.ts` if
  present, and `src/lib/surveys-api.agent-token.test.ts`.
- `src/lib/agent-openapi.ts` and `src/lib/agent-discovery.ts` — this looks like
  the machine-facing API and it matters a lot; describe it precisely.
- `src/app/survey/[slug]/page.tsx` and `src/app/survey/_components/**`
  (`survey-renderer.tsx`, `survey-page-client.tsx`, and the result components).
- `src/app/api/analytics/surveys/**` and `src/lib/analytics/providers/survey.ts`.
- `src/lib/convertkit.ts` and `src/trpc/api/routers/convertkit.ts` where surveys
  touch them.
- Any `src/hooks/use-survey-session-id.ts` equivalent, for anonymous identity.

Answer these, each with file:line evidence:

1. Walk the full lifecycle of one survey: who creates it, in what UI, into what
   storage, and how it reaches a learner's screen. Be a narrative, be exact.
2. **What is the API?** Enumerate the endpoints, their auth (agent token? session?
   admin?), and their request/response shapes. Matt's whole ask hinges on an API
   he can point an agent at. If `agent-openapi.ts` publishes a spec, reproduce
   its operation list.
3. Is a survey a content resource in the same sense as a lesson, or a separate
   table/entity? Show the schema and say plainly which it is.
4. Where does an answer go? Name the table and columns, and say whether it is
   also mirrored to ConvertKit/Kit, analytics, or anywhere else.
5. How is the answering learner identified — session id, cookie, subscriber id,
   authenticated user? Can a logged-out learner answer? What survives a refresh?
6. Is there any correctness, grading, or "you got it right" feedback anywhere in
   this system? Quote the code. If the answer is no, say no clearly.
7. Can a survey question render **inline inside another page's content**, or does
   it require the dedicated `/survey/[slug]` route or the floating widget? What
   would block inline rendering?
8. Note anything that looks abandoned, half-built, or unused — a dead admin
   screen, an unrouted endpoint, a table with no writer.

## Deliverable

Write your findings into this file as a `## Result (2026-07-24)` section.
Lead with a plain-language lifecycle narrative, then the API table, then the
answers to the numbered questions. Set `status: "closed"` and add
`closed_at: "2026-07-24"` to the frontmatter. Cite `path:line` for every claim.
No product recommendations — facts only.

## Result (2026-07-24)

### Lifecycle

An administrator opens `/admin/surveys`; the page requires `manage all`, loads
all `contentResource` rows whose type is `survey`, and exposes create, edit, and
delete controls (`apps/ai-hero/src/app/admin/surveys/page.tsx:8-16`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/surveys-query.ts:222-253`). Creating a survey calls a
server action which writes one `contentResource` row with type `survey`; adding a
question writes another `contentResource` row with type `question` and a
`contentResourceResource` join row that holds its position in the survey
(`apps/ai-hero/src/app/admin/surveys/_components/survey-crud-dialog.tsx:75-94`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/surveys-query.ts:41-82`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/app/admin/surveys/_components/question-crud-dialog.tsx:280-314`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/surveys-query.ts:256-309`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/surveys-query.ts:400-434`). A learner visits
`/survey/[slug]`; the server fetches the survey and ordered question resources,
converts them into the `QuizResource` consumed by `@coursebuilder/survey`, and
renders `SurveyPageClient` (`apps/ai-hero/src/app/survey/[slug]/page.tsx:36-54`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/app/survey/[slug]/page.tsx:88-93`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/surveys-query.ts:184-219`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/surveys-query.ts:506-566`). The client runs the survey
machine, submits known learners per question, or collects an email and submits
all in-memory answers at completion; the tRPC mutations insert one
`QuestionResponse` row per answer and then update Kit subscriber fields when a
subscriber exists (`apps/ai-hero/src/app/survey/_components/survey-page-client.tsx:70-87`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/app/survey/_components/survey-page-client.tsx:98-107`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/app/survey/_components/survey-page-client.tsx:180-194`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/trpc/api/routers/convertkit.ts:273-310`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/trpc/api/routers/convertkit.ts:350-360`).

### API surface

| Surface | Auth | Input | Response |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `GET /api/openapi.json` | Public | None | Generated OpenAPI 3.1 document (`apps/ai-hero/src/app/api/openapi.json/route.ts:6-13`). |
| `GET /api/surveys` | Bearer only: `content:read` personal access token (PAT) or a device token with `read Content`; no browser-session fallback | Optional `slugOrId` returns one survey; optional `search` filters the list (`apps/ai-hero/src/app/api/(content)/surveys/route.ts:25-58`, `apps/ai-hero/src/server/ability-for-request.ts:34-55`). | One `SurveyWithQuestions` object or an array; each survey contains ordered relation rows and nested question resources (`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/surveys.ts:98-128`). |
| `POST /api/surveys` | Device token with `create Content`; scoped PATs cannot write | JSON `{ title, slug?, state?, visibility?, afterCompletionMessages? }` (`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/surveys.ts:67-78`, `apps/ai-hero/src/app/api/(content)/surveys/route.ts:86-107`). | `201` plus the created `SurveyWithQuestions` (`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/surveys-api.ts:137-183`). |
| `PATCH /api/surveys` | Device token with `update Content`; scoped PATs cannot write | JSON `{ id, title?, slug?, state?, visibility?, afterCompletionMessages? }` (`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/surveys.ts:83-95`, `apps/ai-hero/src/app/api/(content)/surveys/route.ts:134-155`). | Updated `SurveyWithQuestions` (`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/surveys-api.ts:186-261`). |
| `DELETE /api/surveys?id=…` | Device token with `delete Content`; scoped PATs cannot write | Required survey id query parameter (`apps/ai-hero/src/app/api/(content)/surveys/route.ts:177-212`). | `{ success: true, surveyId }` after deleting joins, responses, and the survey row (`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/surveys-api.ts:264-311`). |
| `GET /api/surveys/analytics?slugOrId=…` | Device token with `manage all`; `content:read` PAT is excluded | Required id or slug (`apps/ai-hero/src/app/api/(content)/surveys/analytics/route.ts:18-48`). | `{ surveyId, surveySlug, surveyTitle, totalResponses, uniqueRespondents, responsesByDay, topQuestions, recentResponses }` (`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/surveys-api.ts:314-480`). |
| `GET /api/analytics/surveys?range=…` | Device token **or browser session** with `view Analytics` or `manage all` | `range` is `24h`, `7d`, `30d`, `90d`, or `all`; default `30d` (`apps/ai-hero/src/app/api/analytics/surveys/route.ts:23-56`, `apps/ai-hero/src/app/api/analytics/surveys/route.ts:59-83`). | Survey list with response, respondent, and question counts plus links (`apps/ai-hero/src/app/api/analytics/surveys/route.ts:86-165`). |
| `GET /api/analytics/surveys/:id?range=…&limit=…` | Device token **or browser session** with `view Analytics` or `manage all` | Survey id or slug; the same ranges; response limit defaults to 100 and caps at 500 (`apps/ai-hero/src/app/api/analytics/surveys/[id]/route.ts:41-68`, `apps/ai-hero/src/app/api/analytics/surveys/[id]/route.ts:89-96`). | Summary, responses by day, per-question answer distribution, and individual response rows (`apps/ai-hero/src/app/api/analytics/surveys/[id]/route.ts:298-337`). |
| tRPC `convertkit.answerSurvey` | `publicProcedure`; identity is resolved inside the mutation | `{ question: string, answer: string, surveyId?: string }` (`apps/ai-hero/src/trpc/api/routers/convertkit.ts:448-457`). | Updated subscriber, or `{ success: true, storedInDb: true, subscriberLookupError }` when no subscriber exists (`apps/ai-hero/src/trpc/api/routers/convertkit.ts:552-595`). |
| tRPC `convertkit.answerSurveyMultiple` | `publicProcedure`; identity is resolved inside the mutation | `{ answers: Record<string, any>, email?: string, surveyId?: string }` (`apps/ai-hero/src/trpc/api/routers/convertkit.ts:131-140`). | Updated subscriber, or `{ success: true, storedInDb: true, subscriberSyncError }` (`apps/ai-hero/src/trpc/api/routers/convertkit.ts:310-369`). |
| tRPC `convertkit.checkoutSurveyAnswer` | `publicProcedure`; requires a resolvable session/subscriber identity to find a row | None | `{ answered: boolean, answer: string | null }` (`apps/ai-hero/src/trpc/api/routers/convertkit.ts:372-438`). |

The OpenAPI document publishes this full non-preflight operation inventory:
`getVideoResource`; `getLessonSolution`, `updateLessonSolution`,
`createLessonSolution`, `deleteLessonSolution`; `getLessons`, `updateLesson`;
`recallMemory`, `storeMemory`; `getPosts`, `createPost`, `updatePost`,
`deletePost`; `getProductAvailability`; `getProductEnrollment`; `getProducts`,
`createProduct`, `updateProduct`; `getResources`, `updateResource`,
`createResource`; `searchContent`; `createSkillsChangelog`;
`getSurveyAnalytics`; `getSurveys`, `createSurvey`, `updateSurvey`,
`deleteSurvey`; `completeMultipartUpload`, `createMultipartUpload`,
`getMultipartPartUrl`, `createUpload`, `getUploadSignedUrl`;
`listPersonalAccessTokens`, `mintPersonalAccessToken`, and
`revokePersonalAccessToken`. It also publishes named CORS preflight operations
for every listed content path except signed-url and the PAT paths
(`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/agent-openapi.ts:111-504`).

The OpenAPI auth contract says `content:read` grants approved reads, while CMS
writes and survey analytics require an admin device token
(`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/agent-openapi.ts:72-83`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/agent-openapi.ts:330-365`). The runtime request authenticator
reads only the `Authorization` header and recognizes personal access tokens and
device tokens; it does not inspect a browser session
(`apps/ai-hero/src/server/ability-for-request.ts:34-55`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/server/ability-for-request.ts:110-113`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/server/ability-for-request.ts:188-198`). The survey OpenAPI
operations do **not** describe survey request or success schemas: the shared
builder emits an empty success schema, and only PAT minting defines a
`requestBody` (`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/agent-openapi.ts:86-91`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/agent-openapi.ts:449-456`). The REST API has no operation
for question create, update, delete, attach, detach, or reorder; those operations
exist only as authenticated Next.js server actions used by the admin UI
(`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/surveys-query.ts:671-765`).

### Numbered findings

#### 1. Full lifecycle

The lifecycle is the narrative above. The admin list and each detail page require
`manage all`; the detail has Questions, Settings, and Responses tabs
(`apps/ai-hero/src/app/admin/surveys/page.tsx:8-16`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/app/admin/surveys/[slug]/survey-detail-page-data.ts:5-18`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/app/admin/surveys/_components/survey-detail-nav.tsx:8-12`).
The survey and each question are `contentResource` rows, their ordering is a
join-row position, and responses are separate `QuestionResponse` rows
(`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/surveys-query.ts:62-74`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/surveys-query.ts:280-294`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/surveys-query.ts:412-430`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/trpc/api/routers/convertkit.ts:552-559`).

#### 2. What exactly is the API?

The survey-relevant endpoints, auth, inputs, and outputs are in the API table.
The machine-facing discovery path is `/api/openapi.json`; `/api` points agents to
that contract and explains that `aih_pat_*` credentials derive ability only from
their scopes (`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/agent-discovery.ts:304-305`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/agent-discovery.ts:371-389`). A `content:read` PAT can read
survey definitions, including draft/private definitions and questions, but it
cannot create or edit them and cannot read answers or analytics
(`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/agent-openapi.ts:340-365`). Survey write operations require
a device token with the matching Content ability; browser admin sessions do not
authenticate `/api/surveys` (`apps/ai-hero/src/app/api/(content)/surveys/route.ts:86-100`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/app/api/(content)/surveys/route.ts:134-148`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/app/api/(content)/surveys/route.ts:185-205`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/server/ability-for-request.ts:34-55`).

#### 3. Content resource or separate entity?

A survey **is a content resource**, not a separate survey table. `SurveySchema`
merges the generic `ContentResourceSchema` and fixes `type` to `survey`; a
question does the same with type `question`
(`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/surveys.ts:98-112`). Survey-to-question membership is the
generic `contentResourceResource` relation, with `resourceOfId`, `resourceId`,
`position`, metadata, timestamps, and the nested question resource
(`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/surveys.ts:114-128`). Answers are the separate entity:
`QuestionResponse` (`apps/ai-hero/src/db/schema.ts:65-82`).

#### 4. Where does an answer go?

Each answer goes into `QuestionResponse`. Its schema has `id`, required
`surveyId` and `questionId`, optional `respondentKey`, `surveySessionId`,
`userId`, and `emailListSubscriberId`, JSON `fields`, and create/update/delete
timestamps
(`node_modules/.pnpm/@coursebuilder+adapter-drizzle@2.0.0_drizzle-orm@0.36.0_@cloudflare+workers-types@4.202_18bfcf1548b5b2457e0bde6c9a7d7f6e/node_modules/@coursebuilder/adapter-drizzle/src/lib/mysql/schemas/communication/question-response.ts:21-42`).
The current writers store the answer as `fields: { answer: … }`; they set user
and/or Kit subscriber ids but do not set `respondentKey` or `surveySessionId`
(`apps/ai-hero/src/trpc/api/routers/convertkit.ts:273-310`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/trpc/api/routers/convertkit.ts:552-559`).

Answers are also mirrored to Kit when a subscriber resolves. Bulk completion
writes answer keys plus `last_surveyed_on` and
`completed_<survey_slug>_survey_on`; per-question submission calls
`answerSurvey`, which updates a snake-cased subscriber field
(`apps/ai-hero/src/trpc/api/routers/convertkit.ts:157-180`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/trpc/api/routers/convertkit.ts:350-360`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/surveys-query.ts:587-619`). Analytics does not receive a
second answer write: its routes query `QuestionResponse` directly for counts,
distributions, and rows (`apps/ai-hero/src/app/api/analytics/surveys/route.ts:86-105`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/app/api/analytics/surveys/[id]/route.ts:148-184`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/app/api/analytics/surveys/[id]/route.ts:219-285`).

#### 5. Learner identity and refresh behavior

Identity resolution checks the authenticated NextAuth session, then the
`ck_subscriber_id` or serialized `ck_subscriber` cookies, then an input email.
Bulk submission can create a Kit subscriber from that email and can map the
email back to an existing user (`apps/ai-hero/src/trpc/api/routers/convertkit.ts:140-143`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/trpc/api/routers/convertkit.ts:181-216`). The single-answer
mutation follows the same session/cookie/user lookup but has no input-email
field (`apps/ai-hero/src/trpc/api/routers/convertkit.ts:448-500`).

A logged-out learner can open and interact with the dedicated survey because the
route has no auth check and the answer mutations are `publicProcedure`
(`apps/ai-hero/src/app/survey/[slug]/page.tsx:36-54`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/trpc/api/routers/convertkit.ts:131-140`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/trpc/api/routers/convertkit.ts:448-457`). Before email
collection, answers exist only in the client machine. Known subscribers are
written per question; unknown learners are written in bulk when they submit an
email (`apps/ai-hero/src/app/survey/_components/survey-page-client.tsx:98-107`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/app/survey/_components/survey-page-client.tsx:183-194`). The
app has no survey-session hook or dedicated-survey local/session-storage writer
(not found). A refresh therefore rebuilds the client machine rather than loading
saved responses. Database rows already submitted remain, and Kit identity
cookies survive for one year (`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/convertkit.ts:11-30`). The
separate checkout survey is the only AI Hero survey code found using
`localStorage`; it stores one hard-coded checkout answer
(`apps/ai-hero/src/components/commerce/checkout-survey-buy-button.tsx:29-29`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/components/commerce/checkout-survey-buy-button.tsx:68-81`).

#### 6. Correctness and grading

**Yes, correctness feedback exists in the runtime.** The installed survey
question schema has optional `correct` and `answer` fields
(`node_modules/.pnpm/@coursebuilder+survey@1.0.5_@babel+core@7.29.7_@babel+runtime@7.29.7_@codemirror+autoco_b8efe066e4e4b100fa3412abcbc0dade/node_modules/@coursebuilder/survey/src/types.ts:23-31`).
After answer submission, the survey machine goes neutral when `correct` is
empty; otherwise it compares the submitted answer and enters
`answered.correct` or `answered.incorrect`
(`node_modules/.pnpm/@coursebuilder+survey@1.0.5_@babel+core@7.29.7_@babel+runtime@7.29.7_@codemirror+autoco_b8efe066e4e4b100fa3412abcbc0dade/node_modules/@coursebuilder/survey/src/survey-machine.ts:135-173`).
The footer displays the configured neutral, correct, or incorrect message, and
AI Hero renders that footer
(`node_modules/.pnpm/@coursebuilder+survey@1.0.5_@babel+core@7.29.7_@babel+runtime@7.29.7_@codemirror+autoco_b8efe066e4e4b100fa3412abcbc0dade/node_modules/@coursebuilder/survey/src/survey-question.tsx:603-643`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/app/survey/_components/survey-renderer.tsx:118-120`). AI Hero's
DB-to-runtime transform explicitly carries `fields.correct` and `fields.answer`
into the runtime resource (`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/surveys-query.ts:506-555`).

The AI Hero admin question form does **not** expose a `correct` or `answer`
control. Its visible controls cover question, slug, type, dependency, choices,
required, shuffle, and multiple selection
(`apps/ai-hero/src/app/admin/surveys/_components/question-crud-dialog.tsx:343-391`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/app/admin/surveys/_components/question-crud-dialog.tsx:511-607`).
Thus the runtime can grade a question whose stored resource already has
`correct`, but the surveyed admin CRUD path cannot author that field. Separately,
the AI Coding Readiness survey computes a weighted score and profile; that is
survey scoring, not answer correctness
(`apps/ai-hero/src/app/survey/_components/ai-coding-readiness-result.tsx:81-119`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/app/survey/_components/ai-coding-readiness-result.tsx:134-158`).

#### 7. Inline rendering

No current general survey question renders inline inside another content page
(not found). `SurveyPageClient` is used only by `/survey/[slug]`
(`apps/ai-hero/src/app/survey/[slug]/page.tsx:16-16`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/app/survey/[slug]/page.tsx:88-93`). `SurveyRenderer` is reusable
React code, but its interface requires a current question, question id, submit
handler, survey config, machine sender, and completion/email state; the dedicated
client supplies that machinery (`apps/ai-hero/src/app/survey/_components/survey-renderer.tsx:28-52`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/app/survey/_components/survey-page-client.tsx:180-220`). There
is no AI Hero content/MDX registration for it (not found). The checkout screen
does embed one question inside a buy-button flow, but it is a separate hard-coded
question list and separate XState machine, not the data-driven survey renderer
(`apps/ai-hero/src/components/commerce/checkout-survey-buy-button.tsx:25-40`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/components/commerce/checkout-survey-buy-button.tsx:97-115`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/components/commerce/checkout-survey-machine.ts:55-98`).

#### 8. Half-built, unused, or inconsistent surfaces

- The dedicated survey route's published-state check is commented out, so the
  route does not enforce `fields.state === 'published'`
  (`apps/ai-hero/src/app/survey/[slug]/page.tsx:47-51`).
- The admin `deleteSurvey` comment says it deletes the survey and all associated
  questions, but that code deletes only join rows and the survey resource. It
  neither deletes question resources nor `QuestionResponse` rows
  (`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/surveys-query.ts:151-173`). The REST delete path does
  delete `QuestionResponse` rows before deleting the survey
  (`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/surveys-api.ts:289-311`).
- `QuestionResponse` has `respondentKey` and `surveySessionId` columns and a
  uniqueness index keyed by `respondentKey`, but neither current answer mutation
  writes those columns (`node_modules/.pnpm/@coursebuilder+adapter-drizzle@2.0.0_drizzle-orm@0.36.0_@cloudflare+workers-types@4.202_18bfcf1548b5b2457e0bde6c9a7d7f6e/node_modules/@coursebuilder/adapter-drizzle/src/lib/mysql/schemas/communication/question-response.ts:26-59`,
  `apps/ai-hero/src/trpc/api/routers/convertkit.ts:273-310`,
  `apps/ai-hero/src/trpc/api/routers/convertkit.ts:552-559`).
- `src/lib/analytics/providers/survey.ts` instantiates and exports five provider
  methods, but no AI Hero source import of those exports was found; the routed
  analytics surfaces issue their own queries
  (`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/analytics/providers/survey.ts:9-24`,
  `apps/ai-hero/src/app/api/analytics/surveys/route.ts:86-105`).
- The machine-readable OpenAPI advertises only `/api/surveys/analytics`; the
  richer `/api/analytics/surveys` list/detail routes are routed but absent from
  `contentPaths` (`apps/ai-hero/src/lib/agent-openapi.ts:111-418`,
  `apps/ai-hero/src/app/api/analytics/surveys/route.ts:59-64`,
  `apps/ai-hero/src/app/api/analytics/surveys/[id]/route.ts:60-75`).
